-- FG circuit pilot S2s: port of Tools.ShippingChildRunAKids onto the context-predicate bundles (RefLawsAOpsX / RefLawsATeleX); generated by a rename-only script (names + suffix X, `AdmCtx O.quiet` -> `O.adm`). No sorry/axiom/native_decide/TRUSTED/law.

/-! # Row L6: the children of a real core run are `RealChildAX`s (new boundary)

PROVED (relative to `O`, `hA`, the named premises of each statement):
* `closeInstsGM_realCX`: the general closing's children, call by call (origin-built or `RealChildAX`),
  from `BodyStepCX O` (the one-output closing is `Tools.ShippingChildDepthC.closeInstsM_realCX`);
* `synthesizeMachineCertified_runsAX`: a returning run of `synthesizeMachineCertified` from a `JQCX O n`
  world — harness (premise `htr`: the RESTRICTED translator keeps `JQCX O n`, via `mixed_keepsAPX`),
  `closeLets`, closing — has `ChildrenRealAX` children;
* `machine_children_realA'X`: the same for a returning run of the CORE entry from a `JQ O.quiet D` world
  (+ cache half when `D ≠ 0`), through `machine_run_of_coreAX`.

PREMISES (hypotheses, named): `BodyStepCX O` (ComposeC `bodyStepC_of_tele` proves it from `T`);
`htr` (the restricted translator keeps `JQCX O (D + 1)`; ComposeC builds it per step from the handlers);
`MachineClosesAtAX` (the machine synthesis does not fall back — the analogue of the old `MachineClosesAt`).
`ChildrenRealAX` is a HISTORY of past synthesis results, not semantic correctness in the current
environment, and `JQCX` is not freshness. Nothing here is RTL semantic preservation or a runtime-fit proof. -/

